# Container entrypoints and shell scripts MUST stay LF regardless of the host
# git config. A CRLF shebang (`#!/bin/sh\r`) breaks execution inside the Linux
# containers ("no such file or directory"), which would be an intermittent,
# host-dependent failure. Pin the line endings so a Windows checkout can never
# corrupt the built image.
*.sh    text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
